title:: BMSoundFilePlayerGUI
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - GUI class for BMSoundFilePlayer
categories:: Classes

Description::
	
BMSoundFilePlayerGUI creates a gui for a link::Classes/Other/BMSoundFilePlayer::. It provides controls for playback, loading and clearing buffers, and an optional 'Big Clock'. (Click the clock icon.)

See also: link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractGUI::, link::Classes/Other/BMSoundFilePlayer::


CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
Create a new BMSoundFilePlayerGUI.

argument:: player
A link::Classes/Other/BMSoundFilePlayer::.
argument:: name
An optional link::Classes/String:: or link::Classes/Symbol:: indicating the title of the window. If nil is passed the name of player will be used.


INSTANCEMETHODS::

method:: makeBigClock
Open the 'Big Clock' auxiliary window, if not already open. You can also do this by clicking on the clock icon.


Examples::

code::
p = BMSoundFilePlayer(2, name:\foo); // stereo player
p.bus = 0; // for the sake of example
g = BMSoundFilePlayerGUI(p).onClose_({p.free}); // you'll need to load a file
g.makeBigClock // can also click on the clock icon for this
::
